    "background_story": "Marcelo was once a star player on the national soccer team, known for his lightning-fast speed and unmatched skill on the field. However, after a series of injuries, he found himself relegated to the bench, watching as younger, healthier players took his place. Feeling defeated and demoted, Marcelo considered retiring from the sport altogether. But he refused to give up, and instead, he began to focus on coaching and mentoring the next generation of players. He discovered a new passion for teaching and soon became a respected coach, leading his team to several championship wins. Marcelo's experience of being relegated from the spotlight had unexpectedly led him to a new and fulfilling role, one where he could still contribute to the sport he loved, even if it wasn't as a player.",
